This repository contains two kinds of work, under two different licences.

  CODE — the live-quiz platform (labs/live-quiz/), tools/, and the scripts and
  configuration throughout — is under the MIT licence, reproduced below.

  COURSE MATERIAL — worksheets, lab guides, slides, exam papers, CTF briefs and
  the other prose in labs/, slides/, project/ and quizzes/ — is under
  Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International
  (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0). See LICENSE-CONTENT.

  THIRD-PARTY WORK retains its own licence and is listed in NOTICE.

Where a file could plausibly be read as either, the question is what it IS, not
where it sits: a Python module is code even inside a lab directory, and a
worksheet is course material even when it is full of shell commands.

